Confirmed and root-caused: highlights are lost on every save, in every file type. The save boundary ScreenplayFile.encode(_:as:origin:omissions:) re-parses the document's Fountain text instead of writing the editor's live screenplay model, and Fountain cannot spell a highlight — so runs carry bold/italic through but drop highlight silently. Evidence: an eDraft-saved .fdx with an on-screen highlight contains no EDraft:Highlight markup. The engine's reader/writer are fine (FdxRunMarkupTests); the app never reaches them with live runs. Also: an existing EDraft:Highlight in an origin file dies when its paragraph is edited, because the rewrite comes from the Fountain reading too. Do NOT patch this — fold it into the IL-0109/IL-0110 save-boundary refactor: the save must take the editor's live screenplay, not re-parse text. Meanwhile the interim help-text fix (IL-pending, highlights "aren't kept in any file type yet") is approved — ship it, tracked for removal when the real fix lands.